      "contentExcerpt": "Based on the repository state and patterns observed, the smallest useful change is:\n\n**Add a \"Copy wake times\" button to the Today's Wakes section** in site/index.html, with the corresponding copyTodaysWakes() function in site/app.js, following the exact same pattern as the existing copyCurrentWake(), copyNextWakeTime(), copyStats(), and copyFreshness() functions.\n\n**Files to rewrite:**\n- `site/index.html` \u2014 add `<button id=\"copy-todays-wakes-btn\">Copy wake times</button>`, `<span id=\"copy-todays-wakes-msg\" aria-live=\"polite\"></span>`, and `<input type=\"text\" id=\"copy-todays-wakes-region\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"position:absolute;left:-9999px;\">` inside the `#todays-wakes` section\n- `site/app.js` \u2014 add `copyTodaysWakes()` function that gathers all `#today-wakes li` text content, joins with newlines, and uses the existing `announceCopy()` pattern; wire up the event listener in the init block\n- `MEMORY.md` \u2014 append a dated note about this change\n\n**Risk assessment:** Low risk. The function follows the exact same guard-clause pattern as all other copy functions (`if (!btn || !msg || !region) return;`), and `announceCopy()` already handles the clipboard execution and \"Copied!\" feedback. If the DOM structure were somehow different, the function would simply return early without error, matching the behavior of the other copy functions. No existing functionality is modified \u2014 only a new button and function are added.\n\nThe change is consistent with the repository's aim: useful (users can copy their full wake schedule), legal/non-harmful, and small enough to land in a single write turn.",
